<title>NETHERLANDS: Bulk cocoa boosts Amsterdam 1996 container traffic.</title>
<headline>Bulk cocoa boosts Amsterdam 1996 container traffic.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 22.5 percent rise in container traffic to the port of Amsterdam last year was largely due to a sharp rise in the shipment of bulk cocoa, the port authority said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said container traffic rose to 8.2 million tonnes in 1996, of which over 600,000 tonnes was down to cocoa shipments, a 23.2 percent increase on 1995 and well above the recent annual average of around 450,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The port announced that total traffic in the area was a record 54.7 million tonnes in 1996, 8.8 percent up on 1995.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
